---
import ExamQuestion from "./_ExamQuestion.astro";
import Ide from "./_Ide.astro";
import Page from "./_Page.astro";
import {
	PROLOG_BROKEN,
	PROLOG_FAMILY,
	PY_AREA,
	PY_AREA_MODIFIED,
	PY_SNIPPET,
	TERM_DONE,
	TERM_MODIFIED,
	TERM_PROLOG,
	TERM_PROLOG_ERROR,
	TERM_SNIPPET,
} from "./_samples";

export const prerender = false;
---

<Page
  title="Modes"
  lead="The same component in the three places it lives: a code resource in a note, the answer field of an essay question, and the teacher's grading page."
>
  <section class="mt-10">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Snippet: a code resource in a note</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
      Read-only until the reader clicks Edit. The original stays in the note; Reset brings it back. No save state: nothing
      is persisted.
    </p>
    <article class="rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-6">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Week 3: lists and aggregates</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
        Python's <code class="font-mono">sum</code>, <code class="font-mono">max</code> and <code class="font-mono">len</code>
        take any iterable. Combine them to summarize a list of readings:
      </p>
      <Ide class="my-4" mode="snippet" language="python" code={PY_SNIPPET} />
      <p class="text-sm">Change the list and run again. What happens with an empty list?</p>
      <p class="mb-2 mt-6 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">After Edit, then Run</p>
      <Ide mode="snippet" language="python" code={PY_SNIPPET} editing state="done" terminal={TERM_SNIPPET} lastRun="0.4 s" />
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-14">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Answer: an essay question with code content</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
      The IDE replaces the textarea inside the exam question card. Autosave is the exam's existing one; Run never submits.
      The starter code comes from the question (chalk <code class="font-mono">template/</code> later).
    </p>
    <div class="space-y-8">
      <ExamQuestion number={3} title="Rectangle area" points="2.0" saved="saved">
        <p class="text-sm">
          Write <code class="font-mono">area(width, height)</code> and a program that reads both values from the user and
          prints the area.
        </p>
        <Ide mode="answer" language="python" code={PY_AREA} state="done" terminal={TERM_DONE} lastRun="0.3 s" savedAt="14:32" />
      </ExamQuestion>

      <ExamQuestion number={4} title="Family tree" points="3.0" saved="saved">
        <p class="text-sm">
          Define <code class="font-mono">grandparent/2</code> and <code class="font-mono">sibling/2</code> from the given
          <code class="font-mono">parent/2</code> facts. Test them in the toplevel.
        </p>
        <Ide
          mode="answer"
          language="prolog"
          code={PROLOG_FAMILY}
          state="waiting-input"
          terminal={TERM_PROLOG}
          savedAt="14:35"
        />
        <p class="text-xs text-muted">
          Prolog: Run consults the file and opens the toplevel in the terminal; the student types queries there. Stop closes
          it. The toolbar says that Run restarts Prolog, since the toplevel's state is lost.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-1 mt-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">Consult with a syntax error</p>
        <Ide mode="answer" language="prolog" code={PROLOG_BROKEN} state="waiting-input" terminal={TERM_PROLOG_ERROR} savedAt="14:36" />
      </ExamQuestion>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-14">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Review: grading a submission</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
      On the per-question grading page. The teacher runs the student's code as submitted and types into its terminal if
      the program asks. Editing changes an in-memory copy: the box gets a "modified" badge, its output is marked as the
      copy's, and "Back to submission" discards the copy. Previous/Next replaces the whole sandbox.
    </p>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <article class="card card-border bg-base-100">
        <div class="card-body">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-muted">Submission 7 of 27, after the teacher edited line 5</p>
          <Ide
            mode="review"
            language="python"
            code={PY_AREA_MODIFIED}
            state="done"
            terminal={TERM_MODIFIED}
            lastRun="0.3 s"
            modified
            submission={{ index: 7, total: 27, student: "Ana Souza" }}
          />
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="card card-border bg-base-100">
        <div class="card-body">
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-muted">Submission 7 of 27</p>
          <Ide
            mode="review"
            language="python"
            code={PY_AREA}
            state="done"
            terminal={TERM_DONE}
            lastRun="0.3 s"
            submission={{ index: 7, total: 27, student: "Ana Souza" }}
          />
          <form class="mt-4 flex flex-col gap-3">
            <fieldset class="fieldset">
              <label class="label" for="score">Score (out of 2.0)</label>
              <input id="score" class="input w-32" inputmode="numeric" value="2.0" />
            </fieldset>
            <fieldset class="fieldset">
              <label class="label" for="comment">Comment</label>
              <textarea id="comment" class="textarea w-full" rows="2">Correct. Consider validating negative input.</textarea>
            </fieldset>
            <div class="flex gap-2">
              <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary">Save</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost">Cancel</button>
            </div>
          </form>
        </div>
      </article>
      <div class="rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-6">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-muted">Answer key</p>
        <div class="mdq-code mt-2 text-xs">
          <pre><code>def area(width, height):
    return width * height</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
